# PHP release manager public keys, vendored so the build never trusts whatever a
# keyserver hands back at build time.
#
# Every release in matrix.json is signed by exactly one of these keys. The
# table below is the record of which, and scripts/test_release_keys.py asserts
# it stays complete: adding a version to matrix.json without adding its signing
# key here fails that test instead of failing a twenty-minute build at the very
# first RUN with "gpg: Can't check signature: No public key".
#
#   release      fingerprint                               signer
#   php-7.0.33   1A4E8B7277C42E53DBA9C7B9BCAA30EA9C0D5763  Anatol Belski <ab@php.net>
#   php-7.1.33   528995BFEDFBA7191D46839EF9BA0ADA31CBD89E  Joe Watkins <krakjoe@php.net>
#   php-7.2.34   B1B44D8F021E4E2D6021E995DC9FF8D3EE5AF27F  Remi Collet <remi@php.net>
#   php-7.3.33   CBAF69F173A0FEA4B537F470D66C9593118BCCB6  Christoph M. Becker <cmb@php.net>
#   php-7.4.33   5A52880781F755608BF815FC910DEB46F53EA312  Derick Rethans <derick@php.net>
#   php-8.0.30   39B641343D8C104B2B146DC3F9C39DC0B9698544  Ben Ramsey <ramsey@php.net>
#   php-8.1.34   39B641343D8C104B2B146DC3F9C39DC0B9698544  Ben Ramsey <ramsey@php.net>
#   php-8.2.35   E60913E4DF209907D8E30D96659A97C9CF2A795A  Sergey Panteleev <sergey@php.net>
#   php-8.3.36   AFD8691FDAEDF03BDF6E460563F15A9B715376CA  Eric Mann <ericmann@php.net>
#   php-8.4.27   9D7F99A0CB8F05C8A6958D6256A97AF7600A39A6  Calvin Buckley (PHP) <calvinb@php.net>
#   php-8.5.12   D95C03BC702BE9515344AE3374E44BC9067701A5  Daniel Scherzer (for PHP) <daniels@php.net>
#
# Each row was established the same way, and none of it by guessing from a
# name: the fingerprint is read out of the release's own .tar.xz.asc signature
# packet, then confirmed to be published by php.net under that exact branch
# (https://www.php.net/gpg-keys.php), then the key material fetched by full
# 40-hex fingerprint and re-checked -- gpg was asked for that fingerprint and
# the imported key's own fingerprint had to equal it, so a keyserver cannot
# substitute a different key unnoticed. Exported with export-minimal, i.e. no
# third-party signatures.
#
# These are *branch* release managers and a branch has several, so a different
# point release of the same branch may be signed by a different one of them.
# Bumping a release in matrix.json therefore means redoing those three steps
# for the new tarball, not assuming the row above still holds.
#

